 eVTOL Industry's Biggest Customer. Here's How Much Revenue That's Actually Worth to Archer and Joby.","src":"The Motley Fool","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxNazRpZ0t1M1V2S0FDWWxyd0hIV1A2ZUNaZHVqWDZuUTJRRnFRSnJ5S0NvXzRrSjJuSm9sYVJ4WlRNTWRWeWpVSElsaTRLUWRZR3ZfV29ETGhUcGdoZVVFMnlJWmhyVnI4Yy1XOFlvV1NrU0ExM3VqSVpvam11VXNjS2lOS3RzMFBLTFRYd1phLXoxdEJaUTVVbQ?oc=5","date":"2026-10-28","zh":"五角大廈現在是電動垂直起降產業的最大客戶。以下是對阿徹和喬比來說實際上值得多少收入。"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":3},{"name":"訂單/合約","count":3},{"name":"國防/軍工","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-03-02","period":"2025-12-31","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1824502/000182450226000019/achr-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Archer is developing the technologies and aircraft to power the future of advanced aviation. We are building a platform to deliver advanced aircraft, technologies and services to customers worldwide across commercial and defense sectors.","zh":null},{"en":"Midnight is our electric vertical take-off and landing (\"eVTOL\") aircraft purpose-built for air taxi operations globally. To prepare for commercial operations, we are working with aviation authorities, governments, and strategic partners in key U.S. and international markets to certify Midnight and build out air taxi networks. These planned networks will connect major population and business centers with key transportation hubs in select metropolitan areas through partnerships with airline operators to integrate eVTOL flights into passenger journeys and collaborations with infrastructure partners to develop vertiports.","zh":null},{"en":"In the U.S., we have applied to participate in the eVTOL Integration Pilot Program (\"eIPP\"), a White House initiative to accelerate air taxi deployments in American cities. We have partnered with cities across California, Florida, Texas, Georgia, and New York on multiple applications to launch initial air taxi operations under the eIPP later this year. As part of broader commercialization strategy in the U.S., we recently acquired control of Hawthorne Municipal Airport (\"Hawthorne Airport\") located near Los Angeles International Airport and Downtown Los Angeles. We plan for the airport to serve as the operational hub for our Los Angeles network and an innovation hub for developing and commercializing next-generation AI-powered aviation technologies.","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[],"competition":[{"en":"The commercial aerospace and defense industries include many strong U.S. and international competitors. Key competitive factors include long development cycles, rapid technological change, and intense competition. In the defense industry specifically, it is typical to work on development programs in partnership with companies who may also be your competitors and involve a competitive bid process to be awarded a contract.","zh":null},{"en":"In our planned commercial air taxi service, we also compete with ground based alternatives, such as personal automobiles and ride-sharing services, as well as existing aircraft and helicopter charter services. The market for these services is intensely competitive, with key differentiating factors including safety, trip duration, technology, overall user experience, and cost.","zh":null}],"segments":{},"peers":["JOBY","SOUN","BBAI","RKLB","RGTI"]}}